# Google Maps Hackathon Starter

A no-build-step starter (just HTML/CSS/JS) so you can focus on the Maps API
itself instead of tooling.

## Setup (do this before the workshop if you can)

1. **Get an API key**
   - Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
   - Create a project (or use an existing one)
   - Enable these APIs: **Maps JavaScript API**, **Places API**, **Directions API**, **Geocoding API**, **Distance Matrix API**
   - Go to "Credentials" → "Create Credentials" → "API key"
   - Google gives new accounts a $200/month free credit, which is plenty for a hackathon

2. **Restrict your key (recommended, takes 30 seconds)**
   - In the credentials page, click your key → "Application restrictions" → "HTTP referrers"
   - Add `http://localhost:*` and `http://127.0.0.1:*` so it only works from your machine during the workshop

3. **Add the key to the project**
   - Open `index.html`
   - Replace `YOUR_API_KEY_HERE` with your actual key

4. **Run it**
   - You can't just double-click `index.html` (browsers block some Maps features on `file://` URLs)
   - Easiest fix: run a tiny local server from this folder:
     ```
     # Python 3
     python3 -m http.server 8000

     # or, if you have Node
     npx serve .
     ```
   - Then open `http://localhost:8000`

## What's already built

- A full-screen map
- Click the map to drop a marker (click again elsewhere to move it)

## What's not built (that's your job!)

See the `TODO` comments at the bottom of `app.js` for pointers on:
- Adding a Places search bar
- Drawing routes with the Directions API
- Distance Matrix for "nearest X" features
- Custom map styling
- Plotting a data set of multiple points / heatmaps

## Useful docs

- Maps JS API: https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/javascript
- Places API: https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service
- Directions API: https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/directions
- Distance Matrix: https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/distance-matrix